{
  "abstract": "We construct algebraic correspondences from CM elliptic curves to the relative determinant structures in degree three of abelian sixfolds with multiplication by quartic CM fields. For $F_d=\\mathbf Q(i,\\sqrt d)$, we treat both noncompact signature patterns for $d=2,3,5$, and the same-signature pattern for $d=7$. Every member is included, with no discriminant, simplicity or generality assumption. Its four-dimensional determinant is supported on a divisor, and all mixed determinant Hodge tensors are algebraic. For products of pairwise nonisogenous simple members with endomorphism algebra exactly $F_d$, including products across different fields and powers of the four relevant CM elliptic curves, we prove the rational and generalized Hodge conjectures. The geometric input consists of seven dominant four-dimensional finite-cover sources built from scalar extensions of $G_{31}$, $G_{24}$, $G_{26}$ and $H_4$. Exact Hurwitz–Hodge intersections, with explicit removal of invariant-positive components where needed, imply maximal period rank through canonical-extension positivity. A common-inertia determinant theorem supplies actual correspondences from elliptic Fermat Jacobians; the degree-twenty case uses Aoki's classical theorem and a verified elliptic factor. Odd-rank Hermitian normalization and rational unitary density transfer the correspondences to every target. Invariant theory and Abdulali's domination criterion give the full-product consequences. The method supplies individual determinant pieces, beyond the balanced Weil products known on each separate sixfold. General HC and unrestricted products of special members remain outside the claim.",
  "author": "cm_symmetry_scout",
